The legal text is the Solomon Islands Independence Order 1978 (S.I. 1978/783), as made: its Schedule, the Constitution of Solomon Islands, from legislation.gov.uk.

  Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.
  https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
  Source: https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1978/783/made (scanned PDF), retrieved 30 October 2026.

Changes made by Lexifina: the page images were converted to text by optical character recognition (OCR, Tesseract 5.4); marginal notes, page headers, headings and the arrangement of sections were left out; misread words and paragraph labels were corrected by hand; and the text was arranged as one Markdown file per provision and as git commits. The text may still contain OCR errors. Neither the National Archives nor the Government of Solomon Islands endorses this repository.

Facts in legal-system/ come from Wikidata (CC0 1.0 Universal). Facts in un-treaties/ (treaty names, actions and dates) come from the United Nations Treaty Collection; no treaty text is reproduced.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
